    journey="Most trucks spend three or four nights on the road, with halts usually around Dhanbad or Barhi, near Mohania or Varanasi, and near Kanpur or Etawah. NH19 is a wide divided highway for most of its length, and its long chain of toll plazas is added up and shown as one line on the estimate. The Jharkhand section rises gently over the Chota Nagpur plateau and is slower for loaded trucks. From late December to early February, dense fog across Bihar and Uttar Pradesh can cut speeds sharply after dark, so winter loads carry an extra day in the plan.",
    areas="Common delivery areas are Chittaranjan Park, Kalkaji, Greater Kailash, Saket, Vasant Kunj, Dwarka, Janakpuri, Rohini, Pitampura, Mayur Vihar, Noida, Greater Noida West, Indirapuram, Gurugram and Faridabad.",
